    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass (0 failures, 0 errors), including the new `AcceptanceTest`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` is generated from this spec at build time) and updated the field description to document the GOLD rule.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `HOUSEHOLD_GOLD_THRESHOLD` constant (3) and an `applyGoldTier(OwnerDto, Owner)` helper that counts owners sharing the owner's non-null `householdId` and promotes the tier to `GOLD` when the count reaches the threshold. The helper is invoked in both `addOwner` (create response) and `getOwner` (read response), overlaying the SILVER/BRONZE tier the MapStruct mapper already computes.\n\nThe GOLD logic lives in the controller rather than the mapper because the mapper (`OwnerMapper`) is a stateless MapStruct interface with no access to `ClinicService`, which is needed to count the other household members. The existing BRONZE/SILVER computation in the mapper is left untouched and serves as the fallback.",
